hadiths[26]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17271","Yahya ibn Sa'id and Waki' narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seek forgiveness for the front row three times and for the second once."
"17272","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Mu'awiya, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Damra ibn Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Sulami, that he heard al-Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, admonished us with an admonition from which eyes shed tears and hearts trembled, we said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the admonition of a farewellers, so what do you entrust to us? He said: I have left you upon the white path, its night like its day, none strays from it after me but one perished, and whoever lives of you will see much dispute, so upon you is what you knew of my Sunna and the Sunna of the rightly guided rightly guiding caliphs, and upon you is obedience, even if an Abyssinian slave, bite upon it with the molars, for the believer is like the submissive camel, wherever it is led it follows."
"17273","Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us, Mu'awiya, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Sayf, from al-Harith ibn Ziyad, from Abu Ruhm, from Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, invited me to sahur in Ramadan and said: Come to this blessed breakfast."
"17274","al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Thawr, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Sulami, from Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Fajr for us, then turned to us and admonished us an eloquent admonition at which eyes shed tears and hearts trembled, we said, or they said: O Messenger of Allah, as if this is the admonition of a farewellers, so counsel us, he said: I counsel you with fear of Allah and hearing and obedience, even if an Abyssinian slave, for whoever lives of you will see after me much dispute, so upon you is my Sunna and the Sunna of the rightly guided rightly guiding caliphs, and bite upon it with the molars, and beware new matters, for every novelty is an innovation, and every innovation is misguidance."
"17275","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Sulami and Hujr ibn Hujr narrated to us, they said: We came to al-Irbad ibn Sariya, who is of those about whom was revealed: Nor upon those who when they came to you to carry them you said: I find nothing to carry you on, so we greeted and said: We came to you visiting and visiting the sick and seeking knowledge, so Irbad said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Subh with us one day, then turned to us and admonished us an eloquent admonition from which eyes shed tears and hearts trembled, so one said: O Messenger of Allah, as if this is the admonition of a farewellers, so what do you entrust to us? So he said: I counsel you with fear of Allah and hearing and obedience, even if an Abyssinian slave, for whoever lives of you after me will see much dispute, so upon you is my Sunna and the Sunna of the rightly guided rightly guiding caliphs, so hold to it and bite upon it with the molars, and beware new matters, for every novelty is an innovation and every innovation is misguidance."
"17276","Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from Irbad ibn Sariya, that he narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, admonished them one day after the dawn prayer, then he mentioned it."
"17277","Isma'il narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abu Bilal, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, that he narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, admonished them one day after the dawn prayer, then he mentioned it."
"17278","Isma'il narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, that he narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seek forgiveness for the front row three times and for the second once."
"17279","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiya ibn Salih narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Hani, he said: I heard al-Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: I sold a young camel to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then I came to him demanding payment, and said: O Messenger of Allah, pay me the price of my young camel, so he said: Yes, I will only pay you in coined silver, he said: So he paid me and paid me excellently, he said: And a bedouin came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, pay me my young camel, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him that day an aged camel, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is better than my young camel, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of people are the best of them in repayment."
"17280","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Mu'awiya, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Suwayd al-Kalbi, from Abd Allah ibn Hilal al-Sulami, from Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am the servant of Allah, the seal of the prophets, while Adam, peace be upon him, was sprawled in his clay, and I will inform you of the first of that: the supplication of my father Ibrahim, and the glad tidings of Isa of me, and the vision of my mother which she saw, and likewise the mothers of the prophets see."
"17281","Abu al-Ala, who is al-Hasan ibn Sawwar, narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Mu'awiya, from Sa'id ibn Suwayd, from Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal al-Sulami, from Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I am the servant of Allah and the seal of the prophets, then he mentioned the like of it, and added in it: The mother of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw when she bore him a light by which the palaces of Sham were illuminated."
"17282","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiya, meaning Ibn Salih, from Yunus ibn Sayf, from al-Harith ibn Ziyad, from Abu Ruhm, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya al-Sulami, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was inviting us to sahur in the month of Ramadan: Come to the blessed breakfast."
"17283","Then I heard him saying: O Allah, teach Mu'awiya the Book and reckoning and shield him from punishment."
"17284","Abu Asim narrated to us, Wahb ibn Khalid al-Himsi narrated to us, Umm Habiba bint al-Irbad narrated to me, she said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade on the day of Khaybar every taloned bird, the flesh of domestic donkeys, the plundered share, the animal made a target, and that captives be tread until they deliver what is in their wombs."
"17285","Abu Asim narrated to us, Wahb Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Umm Habiba bint al-Irbad narrated to me, from her father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to take a tuft of wool from a heap of the booty of Allah Almighty and say: I have of this only like what one of you has except the fifth, and it is returned among you, so return the thread and the needle and what is above them, and beware misappropriation, for it is disgrace and shame upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Sufyan narrated from Abu Sinan from this Wahb."
"17286","Abd Allah said: Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal is correct."
"17287","Abu Ja'far, who is Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini, narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam informed me, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Khalid ibn Zayd, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When a man gives his wife water to drink he is rewarded, he said: So I came to her and gave her to drink, and told her what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"17288","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, he narrated to him that Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him that al-Irbad narrated to him, and al-Irbad ibn Sariya was of the companions of al-Suffa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray upon the front row three times and upon the second once."
"17289","Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to pray upon the first row three times and upon the one next to it once."
"17290","Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ayyash, meaning Isma'il, narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysara, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Almighty said: Those loving each other for My majesty are in the shade of My Throne on a day when there is no shade but Mine, Abd Allah said: And I think I heard it from him."
"17291","Haywa ibn Shurayh, meaning Ibn Yazid al-Hadrami, and Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, they said: Baqiyya narrated to us, he said: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from Irbad ibn Sariya, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The martyrs and those dead on their beds dispute to our Lord Almighty about those who die of plague, so the martyrs say: Our brothers were killed as we were killed, and those dead on their beds say: Our brothers died on their beds as we died on our beds, so the Lord Almighty says: Look at their wounds, and if their wounds resemble the wounds of the slain, they are of them and with them, and their wounds indeed resembled their wounds."
"17292","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from Irbad ibn Sariya, that he narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to recite the Musabbihat before sleeping, and said: In them is a verse better than a thousand verses."
"17293","al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Damdam ibn Zur'a, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, he said: al-Irbad ibn Sariya said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come out to us in al-Suffa while we wore Hawtakiyya garments, and say: If you knew what is stored for you, you would not grieve over what is withheld from you, and Persia and Rome will surely be opened for you."
"17294","al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed upon the front row three times and upon the one next to it once."
"17295","Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Suwayd, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya al-Sulami, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I am the servant of Allah in the Mother of the Book, the seal of the prophets, while Adam was sprawled in his clay, and I will inform you of the interpretation of that: the supplication of my father Ibrahim, and the glad tidings of Isa to his people, and the vision of my mother which she saw, that a light exited from her by which the palaces of Sham were illuminated for her, and likewise the mothers of the prophets see, the blessings of Allah upon them."
"17296","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from al-Irbad ibn Sariya, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The martyrs and those dead on their beds dispute to Allah Almighty about those who died of plague, so the martyrs say: Our brothers were killed, and those dead on their beds say: Our brothers died on their beds as we died, so Allah Almighty judges between them that: Look at the wounds of the plague-struck, and if they resemble the wounds of the martyrs they are of them, so they look at the wounds of the plague-struck, and they indeed resembled, so they are joined with them."
